                  <div id="negative-words" class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-secondary"></div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <section class="mt-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="text-center mb-8">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-violet-400 uppercase tracking-wider">AI Technology</span><h2
            class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-white mt-1"
          >
            How It <span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-400 to-purple-500 bg-clip-text text-transparent"
              >Works</span
            >
          </h2>
        </div><div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            The AI Sentiment Analyzer uses a <strong class="text-primary">lexicon-based approach</strong> to evaluate the
            emotional tone of your text. It maintains comprehensive dictionaries of sentiment-bearing words categorized by
            emotion type (joy, anger, sadness, fear, surprise) and polarity (positive, negative, neutral).
          </p><p>
            When you analyze text, the engine tokenizes the input and scores each word against these dictionaries. Words
            are weighted by intensity (e.g., "excellent" scores higher than "good"), and negations (like "not good")
            flip the polarity. The overall sentiment is calculated as a composite of positive, negative, and neutral
            scores, visualized in an easy-to-read bar.
          </p><p>
            The emotion breakdown reveals which emotional categories are most present in your text, helping you
            understand not just whether the sentiment is positive or negative, but the specific emotional drivers behind
            it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <ToolContentSections
        toolSlug="ai-sentiment-analyzer"
        toolName="AI Sentiment Analyzer"
        category="AI Tools"
        {benefits}
        howToSteps={howToSteps}
        useCases={useCases}
